# Styling with SCSS

## Core Principles

**SCSS nesting must mirror HTML structure exactly**

Example:
```svelte
<div class="chat-container">
    <div class="message">
        <span class="author">User</span>
        <p class="content">Hello</p>
    </div>
</div>

<style lang="scss">
.chat-container {
    // Container styles
    
    .message {
        // Message styles
        
        .author {
            // Author styles
        }
        
        .content {
            // Content styles
        }
    }
}
</style>
```

## SCSS Best Practices

- **Use SCSS `lang="scss"`** in all Svelte component `<style>` blocks
- **Match HTML hierarchy** - nested selectors should reflect DOM structure
- **4-space indentation** for consistency with code formatting
- **Avoid deep nesting** - max 3-4 levels to maintain readability
- **Use BEM-like naming** for clarity (e.g., `chat-container`, `message-author`)
- **Leverage SCSS features**: variables, mixins, functions when needed
- **Scope styles** - Svelte automatically scopes component styles


## Global Styles

- Minimal global styles in `/src/routes/+layout.svelte`
- Component-specific styles stay in component `<style>` blocks
- Use CSS custom properties (variables) for theming
